{
 "id": "veil-of-ignorance",
 "channel": "philosophy",
 "style": "clay",
 "title": "THE VEIL OF IGNORANCE",
 "angle": "If you had to design a society without knowing who you'd be in it, what would you really choose?",
 "hooks": [
  "Rawls built a thought experiment to protect the unlucky. Real people used it differently.",
  "Eighty-one groups tried John Rawls's famous test. Only one agreed with him."
 ],
 "world": {
  "scenery": "default"
 },
 "script": [
  {
   "text": "Design a whole society. The catch: you don't know who you'll be in it."
  },
  {
   "text": "Rich or poor. Healthy or sick.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "text": "This is John Rawls's veil of ignorance, from 1971.",
   "say": "This is John Rawls's veil of ignorance, from nineteen seventy-one."
  },
  {
   "text": "Rawls knew about luck."
  },
  {
   "text": "At seven, he caught diphtheria, and passed it to his brother Bobby, who died."
  },
  {
   "text": "The next winter, his brother Tommy caught his pneumonia, and died too.",
   "gap": 0.6
  },
  {
   "text": "Behind the veil, Rawls said, you'd make the worst-off life as good as possible."
  },
  {
   "text": "Because it might be yours.",
   "gap": 0.6
  },
  {
   "text": "But economist John Harsanyi had used the same veil earlier, and reached the opposite answer:",
   "say": "But economist John Harshawnyi had used the same veil earlier, and reached the opposite answer:"
  },
  {
   "text": "maximise the average, even if a few lose badly.",
   "gap": 0.6
  },
  {
   "text": "So who's right? Researchers asked real people."
  },
  {
   "text": "Eighty-one groups, in America, Canada and Poland, had to agree on a rule."
  },
  {
   "text": "Only one group chose Rawls's rule. Only ten chose Harsanyi's.",
   "say": "Only one group chose Rawls's rule. Only ten chose Harshawnyi's."
  },
  {
   "text": "About three in four chose a middle path: raise the average, but guarantee a floor.",
   "gap": 0.6
  },
  {
   "text": "In 2019, a Harvard team took the veil into a hospital.",
   "say": "In twenty nineteen, a Harvard team took the veil into a hospital."
  },
  {
   "text": "Taking one patient off oxygen would save nine earthquake victims."
  },
  {
   "text": "Imagining they could be any of the ten, more people chose to save the nine.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "text": "The veil built to protect the unlucky pushed people toward the greater good.",
   "gap": 0.7
  },
  {
   "text": "So if you could be anyone, would you sacrifice the one you might be?"
  }
 ],
